// Manual, editorial exclusions from the playground's catalogue (specification §10.6 —
// this list lives in the site repository, never in the library, which carries no
// showcase-site concern). Each entry needs a non-empty reason.
//
// This file is for exclusions a human chose for a reason the generator cannot see on its
// own. It is NOT how most exclusions happen: the generator (tools/playground-catalogue)
// auto-detects and excludes, with a structural reason, anything it cannot express as a
// flat chain step — an open generic method, a delegate/IAny<T> parameter, a non-array
// collection parameter, a parameter type with no known parser, or a return type that
// isn't itself a chain-eligible IAny<T> builder. Composite generators (Enum<T>, OneOf,
// ListOf/SetOf/DictionaryOf, Combine, PairOf/TripleOf, .As, .OrNull) and constraints
// taking a type nothing here parses (StringMatching(Regex), ...) fall out of that
// automatic classification and never need an entry here.
//
// A `params T[]` of a scalar type is NOT among them: it is catalogued, and asked of the
// visitor as one comma-separated field (Except(...), OneOf(...) — see ArgumentParsing's
// list form). Only its non-params and non-array siblings — a plain T[] parameter, or an
// IEnumerable<T> one such as AnyString.OneOf(IEnumerable<string>) — stay out, each with
// its own automatic reason.
//
// Every auto-detected exclusion is still recorded — see
// packages/playground-catalogue/Generated/PlaygroundCatalogue.Excluded.g.md, written by
// the same generator run, for the full, current, audited list with its reasons.
//
// Matched by the generator's own key format: "{DeclaringTypeName}.{MethodName}", or
// "{DeclaringTypeName}.{MethodName}({ParamType1},{ParamType2},...)" (parameter type
// simple CLR names) when one overload must be excluded but a sibling overload of the same
// name is kept.
[]
